        "worked_solution": "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14093810/assets/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=4,$ $n=5,$ and $n-r=1.$ \n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into $n-r=1,$ we can find the rank of $A:$\n\n$$\n(5)-r=1\\,\u27f9\\,r=4\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}({A}^{T})) & =r=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
